0c14: Si's battle-skill press at 139.68 s (inside the away stretch 134.97–152.91 s) not made, and her press at
153.99 s made though the log shows no hit of it. A MEASUREMENT, hard-coded to the two presses (buffreplay.ts, the
replay's press rule): it sizes the mechanism below; the general rule is the lead's / the replay owner's to build.

The mechanism (damage-factors round, 2026-11-26): the replay made the 139.68 s press as her base battle skill
(`unseen`: no hit could land), so its Artful Intent record, Cryo infliction and Jade Vessel run (enemy-side effects)
went on while the enemy was away, and the 153.99 s press was then Initial Stroke and skipped. In the game the away
press landed on nothing: no Artful Intent burst at its end (the replay's 163.13 s burst_mark is replay-only), no Jade
Vessel on the 152.9–154.2 s hits (the replay's +0.09 DMG taken there reads ×0.92). The 153.99 s press was the base
battle skill: the log lists Jade Vessel's enemy_vul from 155.79 s (the next logged hit after its frame-15 landing),
which only its Immobilization gives, and Artful Intent then ends at the log's 181.00 s (ReplayedCast.expires) with the
burst at 181.42 s. Its Cryo is what Rossi's perfect combo at 165.49 s consumed (a Lift and one more Vulnerable stack:
the log's Airborne and the Endministrator's crystal shatter there, then his Essence Disintegration ATK on the team
165.49–186.28 s), so his Crush at 182.30 s consumed 4 stacks (172,059 = the log's listing at 7.5, exactly), not 2.

Measured (2026-11-26, `--at HEAD --patch <this> --hits`, at c509b8f): only 0c14 moves (earlier pending, mixed):
plain 172 → 293, mismatch 19 → 21, damage −4.9 → +1.2%, mean |per-hit error| 25.9 → 21.0%; the Crush plain, Si's
combo slashes at 167 s plain (4,616), the 165.49 s Airborne and shatter landed. What a general rule needs: (1) a
press whose hits fall in an away stretch applies nothing to the enemy (or isn't made, when its effects are all
enemy-side); (2) a press the log shows no hit of is made when the log lists, from its landing to the next logged
hit, a buff only its hit gives (a cast inferred from a listed buff: Alesh's 12.5 s combo in 0c14 is the other case).

